IdRes.java␀Identifier is not allowed: ␀IdentityHashTable.java␀2If True we are using WebRTC to talk to the server.␀If True, then prompt the user of the WebView to give permission to access the geolocation API. If False, then assume permission is granted.␀PIf enabled is set to true the pull size will be large, else the size is default.␀nIf enabled the arrangement will be convert to a card view. You can detect clicks on it with the "Click" event.␀8If enabled the card layout will have then round corners.␀xIf enabled the dialog will use the color from the "Background Color"-option. Else it will use the theme (light or dark).␀1If enabled the user will see the control buttons.␀HIf enabled you can detect how many faces are in the front of the camera.␀ฉIf enabled you will open the back camera for the camera preview, else you open the front camera. The block detect automatic if there is a device camera available or not.␀VIf enabled you will see a notification in the statusbar after the screenshot is taken.␀YIf enabled you will see a notification with a share button after the screenshot is taken.␀PIf enabled you will see a short preview animation after the screenshot is taken.␀วIf enabled you will see the consent dialog no matter if you are located in Europe or not. Please use this option only in development.  If this setting is enabled ALL taken consents will not be saved.␀<If enabled, then device will listen for changes in proximity␀0If enabled, then device will listen for changes.␀•If enabled, then sensor events will be generated and XAngularVelocity, YAngularVelocity, and ZAngularVelocity properties will have meaningful values.␀TIf false you will see a toast message with a error message when a error is occurred.␀ัIf false, lists will be converted to strings using Lisp notation, i.e., as symbols separated by spaces, e.g., (a 1 b2 (c d). If true, lists will appear as in Json or Python, e.g.  ["a", 1, "b", 2, ["c", "d"]].  This property appears only in Screen 1, and the value for Screen 1 determines the behavior for all screens. The property defaults to "false" meaning that the App Inventor programmer must explicitly set it to "true" if JSON/Python syntax is desired. At some point in the future we will alter the system so that new projects are created with this property set to "true" by default. Existing projects will not be impacted. The App Inventor programmer can also set it back to "false" in newer projects if desired. ␀ยIf set to 1 (OFF) no messages will be received.  If set to 2 (FOREGROUND) or3 (ALWAYS) the component will respond to messages if it is running. If the app is not running then the message will be discarded if set to 2 (FOREGROUND). If set to 3 (ALWAYS) and the app is not running the phone will show a notification.  Selecting the notification will bring up the app and signal the MessageReceived event.  Messages received when the app is dormant will be queued, and so several MessageReceived events might appear when the app awakens.  As an app developer, it would be a good idea to give your users control over this property, so they can make their phones ignore text messages when your app is installed.␀ÞIf set to fixed,  screen layouts will be created for a single fixed-size screen and autoscaled. If set to responsive, screen layouts will use the actual resolution of the device.  See the documentation on responsive design in App Inventor for more information. This property appears on Screen1 only and controls the sizing for all screens in the app.␀(If set to true all states are completed.␀8If set to true justify multiline description is enabled.␀JIf set to true the chat view will scroll down when a new message was send.␀7If set to true the state number is in descending order.␀AIf set to true the states will use a animation when they changed.␀4If set to true the swpipe refresh layout is enabled.␀If set to true the user allowed the ad network to show personalized ads. You only need to request the consent from european users.␀sIf set to true the user will see a dark background effect. Else the background have then no dark background effect.␀VIf set to true the user will see a splash screen while the app is loading the content.␀If set to true will attempt to make text clickable where possible; e.g. hyperlinks, phone numbers. Can not be used for Progress Dialogs. ␀=If set to true you can swipe with your fingers through views.␀KIf set to true you will see a half round circle below the spotlight circle.␀&If set to true you will see system ui.␀[If set to true, it will keep sensing for proximity changes even when the app is not visible␀8If set to true, pictures will be loaded in high quality.␀If set to true, the card will consume all click events. This means if you have added as example buttons into the card, then will the card consume the touch event on the button. And this means that the button would not be clickable, but only the entire card.␀cIf set to true, the device will receive test ads. This option must be set before you load a new ad.␀aIf set to true, the user can use multitouch gestures to rotate the map around its current center.␀*If set to true, user can touch the switch.␀PIf set to true, uses latitude and longitude coordinates as part of an ad request␀7If set to true, you will see tabs above the view pager.␀)If set, button text is displayed in bold.␀,If set, button text is displayed in italics.␀/If set, user can tap check box to cause action.␀(If set, user can touch the radio button.␀pIf the device is currently locked, requests the Keyguard to be dismissed. Works only for devices with Android 8+␀>If the file to be downloaded is to be scanned by MediaScanner.␀ฌIf this property is set to true, multitouch zoom gestures are allowed on the map. Otherwise, the map zoom cannot be changed by the user except via the zoom control buttons.␀cIf true App Inventor will look for and use an external scanning program such as "Bar Code Scanner."␀ปIf true it will show in the TitleBar a back button only if no side menu was added. If a side menu was added it will remove the โ€hamburgerโ€-menu icon but the side menu can still be opened.␀EIf true long click on items are enabled, else long click is disabled.␀GIf true the FAB click listener will be invoked on a text message click.␀QIf true the FAB long click listener will be invoked on a text message long click.␀7If true the first spinner item will be the prompt text.␀AIf true you will see a scrollbar when you scrolling the listview.␀:If true you will see always the scrollbar on the listview.␀กIf true, a separate dialog is used to recognize speech. If false, speech is recognized without changing the user interface and partial results are also provided.␀1If true, an app can retain their older behaviour.␀,If true, the player will loop when it plays.␀vIf true, the player will loop when it plays. Setting Loop while the player is playing will affect the current playing.␀ฑIf true, the player will pause playing when leaving the current screen; if false (default option), the player continues playing whenever the current screen is displaying or not.␀ฺIf true, then SendMessage will attempt to send messages over Wifi using Google Voice.  This requires that the Google Voice app must be installed and set up on the phone or tablet, with a Google Voice account.  If GoogleVoiceEnabled is false, the device must have phone and texting service in order to send or receive messages with this component.␀mIf true, then the listview will show html text else it will show plain text. Note: Not all HTML is supported.␀mIf true, then the subtitle will show html text else it will show plain text. Note: Not all HTML is supported.␀jIf true, then the title will show html text else it will show plain text. Note: Not all HTML is supported.␀lIf true, then this button will show html text else it will show plain text. Note: Not all HTML is supported.␀kIf true, then this label will show html text else it will show plain text. Note: Not all HTML is supported.␀ฎIf true, then this text box accepts multiple lines of input, which are entered using the return key.  For single line text boxes there is a Done key instead of a return key, and pressing Done hides the keyboard.  The app should call the HideKeyboard method to hide the keyboard for a mutiline text box.␀If true, then this text box accepts only numbers as keyboard input.  Numbers can include a decimal point and an optional leading minus sign.  This applies to keyboard input only.  Even if NumbersOnly is true, you can use [set Text to] to enter any text at all.␀มIf true, variables will retain their values when off-line and the App exits. Values will be uploaded to Firebase the next time the App is run while connected to the network. This is useful for applications which will gather data while not connected to the network. Note: AppendValue and RemoveFirst will not work correctly when off-line, they require a network connection.<br/><br/> <i>Note</i>: If you set Persist on any Firebase component, on any screen, it makes all Firebase components on all screens persistent. This is a limitation of the low level Firebase library. Also be aware that if you want to set persist to true, you should do so before connecting the Companion for incremental development.␀ษIf you are having difficulty with the Companion and you are switching between different Firebase accounts, you may need to use this function to clear internal Firebase caches. You can just use the "Do It" function on this block in the blocks editor. Note: You should not normally need to use this block as part of an application.␀eIf you had set your side menu then you can use this block to close it as example with a button click.␀dIf you had set your side menu then you can use this block to open it as example with a button click.␀@If you provide an interpolator, you must set a positive duration␀2If you want to enable the log then set it to true.␀ขIf you want to play live videos you must setup the UI accordingly, by calling this method. If enabled, the user can not select a second on the video progress bar.␀-If you want to subscribe then set it to true.␀xIf you want to test the component then set this property to true and before publishing to Play Store, set back to false.␀bIf you want to test the component then that this property to true. Then you will receive test ads.␀bIf you want to test the component, that this property to true. After it you will receive test ads.␀If-Modified-Since␀If-None-Match␀
