 failed; the device may be out of space.␀nIndicates that an attempt to cache an image resource to the filesystem failed; the device may be out of space.␀SIndicates that an error occurred while communicating with the CloudDB Redis server.␀yIndicates that an unknown server-side error occurred. Note: This code is only possible when working with rewarded videos.␀=Indicates that no ads are currently eligible for your device.␀๔Indicates that the Fusion Tables query has finished processing, with a result.  The result of the query will generally be returned in CSV format, and can be converted to list format using the "list from csv table" or "list from csv row" blocks.␀-Indicates that the SDK is currently disabled.␀+Indicates that the button was pressed down.␀HIndicates that the communication with the Web service signaled an error.␀–Indicates that the developer called for a rewarded video before one was available. Note: This code is only possible when working with rewarded videos.␀~Indicates that the device had no network connectivity at the time of an ad request, either due to airplane mode or no service.␀4Indicates that the gravity sensor data has changed. ␀…Indicates that the gyroscope sensor data has changed. The timestamp parameter is the time in nanoseconds at which the event occurred.␀7Indicates that the impression has already been tracked.␀5Indicates that the magnetic sensor data has changed. ␀’Indicates that the map has been rendered and ready for adding markers or changing other settings. Please add or updating markers within this event␀MIndicates that the network conditions prevented the SDK from receiving an ad.␀iIndicates that the provided ad token is invalid; ad token must be returned from AppLovin S2S integration.␀AIndicates that the recorder has paused, and can be resumed again.␀BIndicates that the recorder has resumed, and can be started again.␀<Indicates that the recorder has started, and can be stopped.␀BIndicates that the recorder has stopped, and can be started again.␀1Indicates that the system is in unexpected state.␀ผIndicates that the user exited out of the ad early. You may or may not wish to grant a reward depending on your preference. Note: This code is only possible when working with rewarded ads.␀5Indicates that the user has clicked on the banner ad.␀8Indicates that the user has clicked on the interstial ad␀Indicates that the zone provided is invalid; the zone needs to be added to your AppLovin account or may still be propagating to our servers.␀BIndicates that there has been a failure to render an ad on screen.␀IIndicates that there was an error while attempting to render a native ad.␀Indicates the current map type␀\Indicates the cursor moved away from the button so it is now no longer possible to click it.␀MIndicates the cursor moved over the button so it is now possible to click it.␀rIndicates whether a collision has been registered between this %type% and the passed sprite (Ball or ImageSprite).␀2Indicates whether a gyroscope sensor is available.␀EIndicates whether a service account should be used for authentication␀QIndicates whether my locaiton UI control is currently enabled for the Google map.␀hIndicates whether network connectivity exists and it is possible to establish connections and pass data.␀OIndicates whether the capability to rotate a map on the ui is currently enabled␀OIndicates whether the capability to scroll a map on the ui is currently enabled␀GIndicates whether the compass widget is currently enabled in the map ui␀7Indicates whether the zoom gesture is currently enabled␀DIndicates whether the zoom widget on the map ui is currently enabled␀,Indicating battery temperature in Centigrade␀#Indicating battery voltage in Volts␀'Indicating whether a battery is present␀XIndicating whether the device is plugged in to a power source. Can be USB, AC or UNKNOWN␀Indie␀IndirectableLocation.java␀
