rticular stream in percent.␀-Sets the volume to a number between 0 and 100␀.Sets the volume to a number between 0 and 100.␀Sets the volume to a number between 0 and 100. Values less than 0 will be treated as 0, and values greater than 100 will be treated as 100.␀>Sets the width of thumbnail in DIP (Density Independent Pixel)␀ฦSets the x and y coordinates of the Ball. If CenterAtOrigin is true, the center of the Ball will be placed here. Otherwise, the top left edge of the Ball will be placed at the specified coordinates.␀8Sets the zoom of the page in percent. The default is 100␀MSets visibility of ShowFilterBar. True will show the bar, False will hide it.␀qSets visibility of ShowSelectionColor. True will show the selection color on a selected item, False will hide it.␀0Sets whether or not to display the slider thumb.␀ÜSets whether the WebView loads pages in overview mode, that is, zooms out the content to fit on screen by width. This setting is taken into account when the content width is greater than the width of the WebView control.␀>Sets whether the WebView requires a user gesture to play media␀?Sets whether the WebView should display on-screen zoom controls␀nSets whether the WebView should enable support for the 'viewport' HTML meta tag or should use a wide viewport.␀4Sets whether the WebView should load image resources␀ZSets whether the WebView should not load resources from the network.Use this to save data.␀^Sets whether the WebView should support zooming using its on-screen zoom controls and gestures␀2Sets whether the WebView supports multiple windows␀ Sets whether to block ads or not␀LSets whether to enable deep links or not i.e. tel: , whatsapp: , sms: , etc.␀6Sets whether to enable text selection and context menu␀#Sets whether to follow links or not␀,Sets whether to load content in desktop mode␀jSets whether webview can access local files.Use this to enable file uploading and loading files using HTML␀Sets whether webview will prompt for permission an